description:
Design a circuit that functions as a buffered input latch. When the enable signal (en) transitions high, the current input value (in) is stored. The output (out) reflects the current input value when en is active. When en is low, the output holds the previously stored input value, effectively enabling the circuit to retain the last valid input state until the next enable pulse.
module top_module(
    input in,
    input en,
    output out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input in,
    input en,
    output out
);reg stored_out;
always @ (posedge en) begin
    if (en) begin
        stored_out <= in;
    end
end

assign out = en ? in : stored_out;

endmodule

