description:
Design a circuit that converts a 4-bit binary input into its corresponding 4-bit Gray code output. The module uses a series of XOR gates to generate the Gray code by comparing bits in the binary input, while also employing AND and NOT gates for intermediate signal generation. The first Gray code bit is directly assigned from the binary input, while subsequent bits are derived from combinations of the binary bits, ensuring that only one bit changes between consecutive values in Gray code format.
module top_module(
    input [3:0] binary,
    output [3:0] gray
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [3:0] binary,
    output [3:0] gray
);// Voltage supply signals
    supply1 VPWR;
    supply0 VGND;

    // Intermediate signals
    wire [3:0] xor_out;

    // Gray code output logic
    assign gray[0] = binary[0];                     // MSB of Gray code is same as LSB of binary
    assign gray[1] = binary[1] ^ binary[0];        // 1st bit of Gray code
    assign gray[2] = binary[2] ^ binary[1];        // 2nd bit of Gray code
    assign gray[3] = binary[3] ^ binary[2];        // 3rd bit of Gray code

endmodule

